messages:
jamal: FWIW with Next edge functions you'll want to avoid Node-only APIs. Edge runtimes (V8 isolates) don't have `stream.Readable` by default. For streaming SDK responses expose both a Web-ReadableStream and a Node-Readable wrapper in the SDK.

Pattern we use:
- Core runtime returns a Web ReadableStream (works in Edge & browsers).
- Provide a small adapter `toNodeStream(stream: ReadableStream) => stream.getReader()` for Node CJS consumers if they expect Node streams.

Example SDK surface:
```ts
// returns Web ReadableStream in both environments
export function streamCompletion(...) : ReadableStream {
  // implementation
}

// adapter
export function webToNode(stream: ReadableStream) {
  const reader = stream.getReader();
  // simple adapter for Node consumers
}
```

We also added runtime detection and exported `streamingSupported: boolean` so apps can fallback gracefully.
